 r←Test_Log_102(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;msg;rc;L;filename;list;expected
⍝ Once the data of a year is saved in "usage-data-YYYY.csv", the monthly files of that year are
⍝ superseded and must be gone; otherwise they are offered as data of the current year.
⍝ Uses data from mid 2022 until 2024-03 to simulate the turn of the year, like Test_Log_100.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 tempDir←∆GetTempDir'-Log/'
 rc←'Create!'F.CheckPath tempDir
 Assert rc
 tempDir ⎕NCOPY ∆TEMP_TEST_DATA,'/LogFile/app-log.txt'
 :For filename :In 'usage-data-2023-11.csv' 'usage-data-2023-11.zip'
     (⊂'Group,Name,Version,Year,Month,Downloads')F.NPUT(tempDir,filename)1
 :EndFor
 L←##.Server.Logs
 L.ProcessLogFile tempDir(2024 3 4)

 →T.GoToTidyUp 0<≢F.ListFiles tempDir,'usage-data-2023-*'
 list←{⊃,/1↓⎕NPARTS ⍵}¨F.ListFiles tempDir,'usage-data-20*.csv'
 expected←'usage-data-2022.csv' 'usage-data-2023.csv' 'usage-data-2024-02.csv'
 →T.GoToTidyUp~list ∆LazyMatch expected

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←F.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
